n the path becomes 2, so the path continues the marker colour;\n- a 1 on the path becomes 3, marking where the line crosses a 1.\n\nThe counts confirm this:\n- Pair 1: the 10 interior cells of row 8 split into 0→2 ×5 and 1→3 ×5.\n- Pair 2: the 14 interior diagonal cells split into 0→2 ×11 and 1→3 ×3.\n- Pair 3: the 8 interior column cells split into 1→3 ×5 and 0→2 ×3.\n\nThe mapping 0→2 and 1→3 holds in all three pairs. In the test the most common colour is 1 rather than 0. The rule depends on cell values, not on the background, so the same mapping still applies.\n\n**Construction.**\n1. Find the two 2-cells.\n2. Compute the step between them, which is the sign of dy and the sign of dx. This gives a row, column or diagonal direction.\n3. Walk from the first marker towards the second. Recolour each interior cell: 0 becomes 2 and 1 becomes 3.\n\n**Test input.** The markers are at (0,17) and (17,0), on the anti-diagonal. The step is (+1,−1). Each of the 16 interior anti-diagonal cells is recoloured according to its value.\n\n**Teaching stages.** The program emits the canvas once after marking the first half of the path. It then emits the finished canvas.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    pts = sorted(zip(*np.where(g == 2)))\n    (y0, x0), (y1, x1) = pts[0], pts[-1]\n    dy = int(np.sign(y1 - y0)); dx = int(np.sign(x1 - x0))\n    n = max(abs(y1 - y0), abs(x1 - x0))\n    half = (n - 1) // 2\n    for k in range(1, n):\n        y, x = y0 + k * dy, x0 + k * dx\n        if g[y, x] == 0:\n            g[y, x] = 2\n        elif g[y, x] == 1:\n            g[y, x] = 3\n        if k == half and half > 0:\n            emit(g, \"Walking from the first 2-marker toward the second: path cells so far recoloured (0->2, 1->3).\")\n    emit(g, \"Completed the straight line between the two 2-markers: empty cells became 2, crossed 1-cells became 3.\")\n    return g\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"In the test the most common colour is 1 rather than 0."}],"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Recolour each interior cell: 0 becomes 2 and 1 becomes 3."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each of the 16 interior anti-diagonal cells is recoloured according to its value."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Walking from the first 2-marker toward the second: path cells so far recoloured (0->2, 1->3)."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 1: the 10 interior cells of row 8 split into 0→2 ×5 and 1→3 ×5."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 2: the 14 interior diagonal cells split into 0→2 ×11 and 1→3 ×3."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 3: the 8 interior column cells split into 1→3 ×5 and 0→2 ×3."}],"paths":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- a 0 on the path becomes 2, so the path continues the marker colour;"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- a 1 on the path becomes 3, marking where the line crosses a 1."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Teaching stages.** The program emits the canvas once after marking the first half of the path."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The counts confirm this:"}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"307329c2359a89e61a661d5c9f93015ffc3c2946a4eb8d92af4a6d82a47c19c6","task_sha256":"8cb127484a0f19a055dd3652fc48671983b965953f9fdc82eff6c20e6ff0be54","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
